{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I fetch a URL with requests?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport requests\n\nresp = requests.get(\"https://api.github.com\")\nprint(resp.json())\n```"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Now fetch 10 URLs concurrently."}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "Use a thread pool since `requests` is blocking:\n\n```python\nimport requests\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n\nurls = [f\"https://api.github.com/users/user{i}\" for i in range(10)]\n\ndef fetch(url):\n    return requests.get(url).json()\n\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=10) as ex:\n    results = list(ex.map(fetch, urls))\nprint(len(results))\n```"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Add a timeout and error handling."}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport requests\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n\nurls = [f\"https://api.github.com/users/user{i}\" for i in range(10)]\n\ndef fetch(url):\n    try:\n        resp = requests.get(url, timeout=5)\n        resp.raise_for_status()\n        return resp.json()\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        return {\"error\": str(e), \"url\": url}\n\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=10) as ex:\n    results = list(ex.map(fetch, urls))\nfor r in results:\n    print(r)\n```"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Write a simple async function that sleeps and returns a value."}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def work():\n    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n    return 42\n\nprint(asyncio.run(work()))\n```"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Run three of them concurrently."}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def work(n):\n    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n    return n\n\nasync def main():\n    return await asyncio.gather(work(1), work(2), work(3))\n\nprint(asyncio.run(main()))\n```"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Limit it so only two run at a time."}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def work(sem, n):\n    async with sem:\n        await asyncio.sleep(1)\n        return n\n\nasync def main():\n    sem = asyncio.Semaphore(2)\n    return await asyncio.gather(*(work(sem, i) for i in range(6)))\n\nprint(asyncio.run(main()))\n```"}]}
