{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I run multiple independent asyncio coroutines that loop forever?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def ticker(name, interval):\n    while True:\n        print(name)\n        await asyncio.sleep(interval)\n\nasync def main():\n    await asyncio.gather(\n        ticker(\"fast\", 1),\n        ticker(\"slow\", 3),\n    )\n\nasyncio.run(main())\n```"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I send concurrent POST requests with aiohttp?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport aiohttp\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def post(session, payload):\n    async with session.post(\"https://httpbin.org/post\", json=payload) as resp:\n        return await resp.json()\n\nasync def main():\n    async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session:\n        payloads = [{\"id\": i} for i in range(5)]\n        return await asyncio.gather(*(post(session, p) for p in payloads))\n\nresults = asyncio.run(main())\nprint(len(results))\n```"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I handle an aiohttp request error?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport aiohttp\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def fetch(url):\n    async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session:\n        try:\n            async with session.get(url) as resp:\n                resp.raise_for_status()\n                return await resp.text()\n        except aiohttp.ClientResponseError as e:\n            return f\"HTTP {e.status}\"\n        except aiohttp.ClientError as e:\n            return f\"client error: {e}\"\n\nprint(asyncio.run(fetch(\"https://httpbin.org/status/404\")))\n```"}]}
