{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I retry a failed request with exponential backoff?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport time\nimport requests\n\ndef get_with_backoff(url, retries=4):\n    for attempt in range(retries):\n        try:\n            resp = requests.get(url, timeout=5)\n            resp.raise_for_status()\n            return resp\n        except requests.exceptions.RequestException:\n            if attempt == retries - 1:\n                raise\n            time.sleep(2 ** attempt)  # 1, 2, 4, ...\n\nprint(get_with_backoff(\"https://example.com\").status_code)\n```"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain producer/consumer pattern."}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "Producers create work items and put them on a shared queue; consumers take items off and process them. The queue decouples their speeds and provides backpressure. In asyncio you use `asyncio.Queue`; with threads you use `queue.Queue`; both are safe for concurrent access."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I gracefully shut down an asyncio server on Ctrl+C?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def main():\n    try:\n        while True:\n            await asyncio.sleep(1)\n            print(\"running\")\n    except asyncio.CancelledError:\n        print(\"cleaning up\")\n\ntry:\n    asyncio.run(main())\nexcept KeyboardInterrupt:\n    print(\"shutdown\")\n```"}]}
