{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I share an asyncio.Semaphore across functions cleanly?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "Create it once in your entry coroutine and pass it down, or store it on a shared object:\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def limited(sem, n):\n    async with sem:\n        await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n        return n\n\nasync def main():\n    sem = asyncio.Semaphore(5)\n    return await asyncio.gather(*(limited(sem, i) for i in range(20)))\n\nprint(len(asyncio.run(main())))\n```"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I do a HEAD request asynchronously to check a URL exists?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport aiohttp\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def exists(url):\n    async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session:\n        async with session.head(url) as resp:\n            return resp.status < 400\n\nprint(asyncio.run(exists(\"https://example.com\")))\n```"}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "How do I batch a large list of items for processing in asyncio?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def process(batch):\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n    return sum(batch)\n\nasync def main(items, size=10):\n    batches = [items[i:i+size] for i in range(0, len(items), size)]\n    return await asyncio.gather(*(process(b) for b in batches))\n\nprint(asyncio.run(main(list(range(100)))))\n```"}]}
